<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent liftings up sharply last week.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent liftings up sharply last week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent crude from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal fell sharply to 500,995 tonnes in the week to September 24 from 1,004,205 tonnes the previous week, the Shetland Islands Council Marine Operations Department said.</p>
<p>One cargo of 131,800 tonnes went to the U.S., compared to a total of 372,149 tonnes the previous week.</p>
<p>Below is a list of loadings:</p>
<p>DATE     VESSEL		    DESTINATION	CARGO (TONNES)</p>
<p>18/9     Alandia Pearl	   Gdansk	     69,224</p>
<p>19/9     Windsor		   Shell Haven, UK  69,198</p>
<p>23/9     Sunetta		   Hamburg	    69,207</p>
<p>	   Nikator		   U.S. Gulf	 131,800</p>
<p>	   Sanko Protector	 Fawley, UK	 92,337</p>
<p>	   Alandia Tide	    Tranmere, UK     69,229</p>
<p> WK ENDING   U.K.     NWE   AMERICAS  MED    OTHER	 TOTAL</p>
<p> 24/9     230,764  138,431  131,800   --	--	 500,995</p>
<p> 17/9     397,164  234,892  372,149   --	--     1,004,205</p>
<p> 10/9     214,529  217,659   --	 --	--	 432,188</p>
<p>  3/9     297,770  201,977  176,684   --	--	 676,431</p>
